# Everything under bin/ is phone firmware or a compiled binary, and git must
# not touch a byte of any of it.
#
# This is not a tidiness setting. core.autocrlf is on for most Windows clones,
# and git decides what is text by sniffing the first few kilobytes for a NUL.
# A ROM image or an .rsc resource can easily open with a stretch that has none,
# at which point every 0x0A in seventy megabytes of ARM code becomes 0x0D 0x0A
# on checkout and the clone gets firmware that will not boot - silently, and
# only for the people who cloned rather than built.
bin/** binary

# dist/ is ignored rather than committed - the installer is attached to its
# release instead - but if one is ever forced in, it is not text either.
dist/** binary
